\par\par \b \uc2 Romania - Factors to Watch on July 12   \b0\par\par\uc2 563 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2007\par 08:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, July 12 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Romanian financial markets on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 EU FUNDS AGREEMENT   \par \par \uc2 Romanian Prime Minister Calin Tariceanu and European Commissioner for Regional Policy Danuta Hubner will sign an agreement concerning the new EU member's strategic framework for absorbtion of EU funds.   \par \par \uc2 CONFERENCE ON EU STRUCTURAL FUNDS   \par \par \uc2 European Commissioner for Regional Policy Danuta Hubner and Romanian Finance and Economy Minister Varujan Vosganian open a two-day conference on EU structural funds for the new bloc member.   \par \par \uc2 NO \b \highlight22\uc2 ROMANIA FX INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  RECENTLY-CBANK ECONOMIST   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in recent days to curb a strong appreciation of the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , chief economist Valentin Lazea said on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL11822304]   \par \par \uc2 ROMANIA SELLS 139 MLN LEI IN 6-MONTH T-BILLS   \par \par \uc2 Romania sold 139 million lei ($61.02 million) worth of 6-month T-bills at an auction on Wednesday, with the average accepted yield at 6.83 percent against 6.05 percent at a previous tender on Feb. 12.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nBUC000749]   \par \par \uc2 ROMANIAN PENSION CHIEF SEES ENOUGH CASH FOR HIKES   \par \par \uc2 Romania may be able to fund a 7 billion lei pension hike next year with little help from the state budget, relying largely on measures to raise the collection of social insurance contributions, a senior official said on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL11815773]   \par \par \uc2 GOVT TO SHOW PRESIDENT PENSION HIKE MONEY NEXT WEEK   \par \par \uc2 The government will answer next week to a request from President Traian Basescu to explain its strategy for funding increases in state pensions that will almost double them in two years. The strategy should also include social insurance budget forecasts until 2013.   \par \par \uc2 Evenimentul Zilei, Page 1   \par \par \uc2 C.BANK SAYS PENSION HIKES SHOULD NOT WEIGH ON CPI   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesperson Mugur Stet said a plan to nearly double state pensions in two years will not impact inflation significantly, as long as the hikes will not lead to unbalances in the social insurance budget and a rise in the consolidated budget deficit.   \par \par \uc2 Ziarul Financiar, Page 2   \par \par \uc2 A second unit at Romania's sole nuclear power plant in Cernavoda will be connected to the national grid by the end of July and become fully functional in September, said the general director of the plant's operator, Nuclearelectrica.   \par \par \uc2 The two units will provide roughly 19 percent of the country's emergy production.   \par \par \uc2 Ziarul Financiar, Page 3   \par \par \uc2 ING BANK MAY MAKE ACQUISITION IN ROMANIA-ING BANK ROMANIA   \par \par \uc2 ING Bank is considering making an acquisition in Romania, as it moves to expand in Southeast Europe and Asia, but plans are not yet concrete, said the general director of  \uc2 ING Bank Romania.\par \par \uc2 Ziarul Financiar, Page 6   \par \par \uc2 NOTE - For a diary of forthcoming Romanian events, double click [RO/DIARY], and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see [CONV/DIARY].   \par \par \uc2 For other related news, double click on:    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  Romania Market Debt     [RO-DBT]   Romanian \f28 \b \highlight22