\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  talk briefly hurts buoyant leu   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Marius Zaharia and Luiza Ilie   \par \uc2 425 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2007\par 11:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, quotes)   \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, April 27 (Reuters) - The Romanian leu lost one percent against the euro on Friday, sliding away from its highest level in nearly five years amid speculation of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , later denied by the bank.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebounded in later trade as investors rebuilt positions in line with broadly positive sentiment towards the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is benefiting from strong economic growth prospects in the wake of Romania's European Union entry.   \par \par \uc2 "At some point, we all knew it was just a rumour and this made the leu recover," said a dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest. "The rumour was spread by somebody from the market and he took good profit from it."   \par \par \uc2 The leu fell as low as 3.3350 per euro <EURRON=>, compared to highs of around 3.30 which it hit on Thursday and tested again on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 By 1215 GMT, it had recovered some ground to trade at 3.3098/58.   \par \par \uc2 "You get scared at some point, but after several minutes you realise the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had no reason to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . If the leu is on an emerging markets firming trend, an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't hold it from firming but for a few hours," a dealer said.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  openly in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in late 2005, when it tried to bring down a soaring leu. Before Friday's speculation, it said it had not been in the market since.   \par \par \uc2 But it has said interest rate cuts this year were in part driven by concerns that a rapid leu rise posed a threat of a sharp reversal that could reignite inflation.   \par \par \uc2 On Friday, the bank's spokesman Mugur Stet told Reuters:   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. (Today's) evolution of the leu's exchange rate is not related to the presence of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market."   \par \par \uc2 The leu is supported by investors' optimism towards Romania which joined the European Union this year, and prospects for strong inflows of direct investment and EU cash.   \par \par \uc2 Its latest surge was also helped by a jump in overnight money market rates to their highest level since January 2005 at 28.50/54.13 percent.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the spike in rates followed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move this week to drain more liquidity from the market than expected.   \par \par \uc2 ROMANIA-MARKETS/LEU (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|RDN|GNN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070427e34r0019f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
