\par\par \b \uc2 Romania - Factors to Watch on May 26  \b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Mai 2006\par 07:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, May 26 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Romanian financial markets on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 CBANK: LIMITED REASONS FOR \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  INTERVETION  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to protect "financial stability" and thereby its efforts to curb inflation, governor Mugur Isarescu said on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL25743547]  \par \par \uc2 ENERGY TARIFFS TO RISE FROM JULY  \par \par \uc2 The government plans to hike electricity and gas tariffs by 1-2 percent from July 1, Economy Minister Codrut Seres was quoted as saying.  \par \par \uc2 Ziarul Financiar, page 1  \par \par \uc2 BULGARIA BANS ROMANIAN POULTRY OVER BIRD FLU  \par \par \uc2 Bulgaria said it would ban poultry products from its northern Black Sea neighbour Romania on Thursday after the discovery of dozens of new cases of avian flu there.  \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL25516603]  \par \par \uc2 ALTEX REPORTS 47 MLN EUROS TURNOVER IN Q1  \par \par \uc2 Electronics retailer Altex reported in the first quarter of the year a turnover of 47 million euros ($59.99 million), 8 percent down from in the same 2005 period.  \par \par \uc2 Ziarul Financiar, page 1  \par \par \uc2 POLUS TO BUILD 115 MLN EURO SHOPPING MALL  \par \par \uc2 Polus Transilvania will invest around 115 million euros in a commercial centre in the Black Sea county of Constanta.  \par \par \uc2 Ziarul Financiar  \par \par \uc2 NOTE - For a diary of forthcoming Romanian events, double click [RO/DIARY], and a calendar of east European econ