\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2  cbank: limited reasons for  \highlight22\uc2 fx intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 417 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2006\par 13:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, May 25 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to protect "financial stability" and thereby its efforts to curb inflation, governor Mugur Isarescu said on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The bank, which started to target inflation rates in 2005, has come under heavy criticism from foreign observers such as the IMF for weakening its anti-inflation efforts by curbing the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Everybody looks at the exchange rate ... the exchange rate has a visibility and a big impact on the economy," Isarescu told a financial seminar.  \par \par \uc2 "If we \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  that means that we are protecting financial stability...This way we give sustainability to disinflation," Isarescu said.  \par \par \uc2 Inflation fell to a post-communist low of 6.9 percent on the year in April and is widely expected to rise in coming months due to tax hikes, before subsiding slightly later this year.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has recently raised its end-year forecast to 6.8 percent from 6.5 percent, further above its December target of 4-6 percent. It expects inflation to move within its 3-5 percent goal next year.  \par \par \uc2 It raised its key rate by 100 basis points to 8.5 percent in a surprise move in February to keep inflation at bay.  \par \par \uc2 But it kept credit costs on hold for two meetings in a row afterwards, including earlier this month, with some analysts saying its inflation-fighting credibility was on the line because of expectations of higher price growth in coming months.  \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Isarescu said the fight against inflation is safe from any impact of this month's sharp fall in the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the euro.  \par \par \uc2 The leu <EURRON=> has hit its lowest level against Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since early February as other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumbled while the euro gained across the board.  \par \par \uc2 Isarescu reiterated that his bank has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since last autumn. "We did not have a free float (regime), we did not declare that the exchange rate is perfectly free. However, over the past seven months we haven't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Isarescu said.  \par \par \uc2 "We have a managed float which implies that we maintain the right (to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) when conditions go against what the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wishes."  \par \par \uc2 A free float would imply a commitment by the bank to refrain for ever from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said, adding "We are not there."  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-\b \highlight22\uc2 ROMANIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -C.BANK|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RDN|GNN|BNX|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060525e25p000zd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
