\par\par \b \uc2 Romanian leu retreats, c.bank keeps  \highlight22\uc2 intervening \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 372 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2005\par 16:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Sept 28 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's leu <EURRON=> lost 0.4 percent to the euro on Wednesday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) continued fighting its rise with \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while keeping the money market flooded with excess liquidity, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The BNR entered the market directly for the second day running on Wednesday to stop the leu's surge in what traders said was a moderate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , knocking the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 3.5450 per euro.  \par \par \uc2 The leu failed to recover from the slide, ending at 3.5430/00, compared with Tuesday's close of 3.5300/70.  \par \par \uc2 Market watchers said the BNR's Wednesday action signalled it probably wanted to lock the leu in a range of 3.5400 and 3.5500 per euro for the foreseeable future.  \par \par \uc2 "The BNR popped up on dealing screens a couple of times this morning without drawing any significant amounts, entrenching, however, a sentiment that it would not allow the RON to find its way near 3.5000 (per euro)," Piraeus Bank said in a market note.  \par \par \uc2 The leu plunged 2.5 percent to the euro last week, giving up most of its gains over the past three months following the BNR's one-percentage-point cut to the main policy rate, which brought it to 7.5 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The unit regained ground earlier this week as foreign players boosted exposure in the EU candidate's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and corporates sold euros to settle their end-month payments.  \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the BNR carried no open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , leaving interbank rates under pressure. The short-term rates remained stable at 1.2/4.8 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The BNR left banks struggling to place excess funds over the past weeks, squeezing interbank rates to levels unseen since the fall of communism in 1989 to discourage speculators from boosting the leu.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  computed the indicative rate of the leu <FXRO01> at 3.5422 to the euro and 2.9488 to the dollar. The rate is not compulsory for book-keeping or interbank deals. It is used by the Finance Ministry and customs for statistical purposes.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ROMANIA-LEU|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|RBN|RDN|GNN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050928e19s001b2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
