\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Romania central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2  to cap leu rise  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Martin Dokoupil and Radu Marinas  \par \uc2 454 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2005\par 13:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealer's comment, background)  \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Sept 27 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday, buying euros to slow down the surging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fuelled by renewed interest from foreign investors, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The BNR has stepped in several times in recent months to rein in the leu despite its shift to inflation targeting from August to fight rising prices in the EU candidate, saying it would not allow excessive exchange rate moves.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said on Tuesday, the BNR started to buy euros at around 3.5180 leu per euro. "It used only very small banks to buy from," said a dealer in Bucharest.  \par \par \uc2 BNR officials, who rarely talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , declined to comment: "We do not make any comments about our presence in the market," BNR spokesman Mugur Stet said.  \par \par \uc2 The leu had been under pressure last week, loosing 2.5 percent to the euro - nearly all of its gains since its July introduction - after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  slashed its policy rate by 100 basis points to 7.5 percent, citing slowing inflation.  \par \par \uc2 The unit rebounded quickly this week to climb as far as 3.5 per euro on Tuesday, as foreign players and local corporates dumped euros, prompting the BNR to step in, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <EURRON=> eased to levels of around 3.5400 per euro after the BNR action, but later recovered slightly to end at 3.5300/70. It closed at 3.5390/40 on Monday.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said the BNR, which was estimated to have bought around 20 million euros in its Tuesday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , would probably try to prevent the leu from crossing the 3.5 per euro level in the near future.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't think they'll let it linger too much too close to 3.5000 (per euro). However, it's the month end now and usually clients sell (euros) in this period," said Piraeus Bank dealer Valentin Ciobotaru.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  carried no open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, after draining 3.0 billion lei worth of one-month deposits on Monday in what analysts said was too little to reduce a huge liquidity surplus on the money market.  \par \par \uc2 The BNR had refrained from calling the tender for the previous four weeks, driving interbank rates to levels unseen since the fall of communism in 1989 to prevent hot-money inflows from boosting the leu.  \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the short-term rates ticked up to 1.2/4.8 percent from 1.0/4.2 percent on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ROMANIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RDN|GNN|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050927e19r0013e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
