\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2  c.bank keeps fighting leu rise,  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Martin Dokoupil  \par \uc2 482 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2005\par 11:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds c.bank, analyst comments, background)  \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Sept 14 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market again on Wednesday to slow down the leu's rise, but analysts said players' attempts to push the unit stronger would probably continue in the coming days.  \par \par \uc2 The BNR has bought euros several times in recent months to rein in the leu despite its shift to inflation targeting, saying it would not allow excessive exchange rate moves. It also left the money market flooded with liquidity to deter hot money inflows.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the bank's latest move indicated that the BNR, which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on Monday and may have bought small amounts of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, probably wanted to stabilise the leu at around 3.5 to the euro.  \par \par \uc2 "It \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  when bids hit a high of 3.4830 (per euro)," said one dealer with a commercial bank.  \par \par \uc2 The leu <EURRON=> weakened as far as 3.4980 per euro after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but later recovered slightly to close at 3.4938/40, down from 3.4870/20 on Tuesday. This compares with a two-and-half year high of 3.4000 it hit in mid-August.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which rarely speaks about its exchange rate policy moves, declined to comment: "We do not comment on our \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," spokesman Mugur Stet said.  \par \par \uc2 The Balkan country's policymakers turned to inflation targeting last month, but said they would keep managing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements when needed in future.  \par \par \uc2 The leu has gained more than three percent since July, buoyed by remittances from workers abroad and by speculative inflows after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  relaxed its grip on the market following a move to slash four zeroes off the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said investors would keep playing on BNR nerves in the near term as more firming was in the pipeline due to a recent rating upgrade by Standard & Poor's and expectations of FDI inflows from privatisations in the banking sector.  \par \par \uc2 "I am sure they (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) would be very happy to stabilise the exchange rate at 3.50 or 3.60 (per euro) ... but given the strong flows they might not be successful," said Agata Urbanska, emerging Europe economist at ING Financial Markets in London.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts expect the leu to stand anything between 3.21 and 3.75 per euro at the end of the year.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers estimated the BNR had bought between 25 and 50 million euros in Wednesday \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , down from 100 million in its previous action on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, short-term market rates were unchanged at 3.28/6.47 percent. The BNR carried no open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  <BNR16>. (Additional reporting by Antonia Oprita)  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ROMANIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RDN|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050914e19e000t6\par }\pag