\par\par \b \uc2 Romanian leu weakens vs euro after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 384 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2005\par 15:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Sept 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's leu <EURRON=> closed weaker against the euro on Monday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to stem its fast rise, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The leu ended at 3.4920/70 against Friday's 3.4700/40.  \par \par \uc2 The central (BNR) bank moved in to buy euros in morning trade, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly and via commercial banks when the leu was trading at 3.4760 bid, and brought it down to 3.5000, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Some dealers said the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in afternoon trade, when the leu had risen to 3.4800/70 to the euro.  \par \par \uc2 "I think overall it bought around 100 million euros from the market today," said one dealer with a foreign bank.  \par \par \uc2 It was the first time the bank stepped into the market after last month's repeated attempts to tame the leu, just after announcing a switch to inflation targeting to fight rising prices as Romania moves closer to EU membership in 2007.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers and analysts had expected the bank to step into the market as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed last week, fuelled by export-related and some speculative hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows.  \par \par \uc2 Traders saw the leu stable on Tuesday but continuing to firm towards the middle of the week unless the BNR drains hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  again.  \par \par \uc2 "I think it (the BNR) wants to keep it between 3.4900 and 3.5000, but maybe later in the week the leu will appreciate towards 3.4500," said one dealer.  \par \par \uc2 They said official data showing year-on-year inflation slowing to 8.9 percent in August from July's 9.3 percent had no impact on trading as it was widely expected.  \par \par \uc2 Short-term market rates were 2.0/4.0 percent from Friday's 3.8/6.9 percent. The BNR had no open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  <BNR16>.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  computed the indicative rate of the leu <FXRO01> at 3.4978 to the euro from 3.4851 on Friday. It was 2.8377 to the dollar from 2.8109. The rate is not compulsory for book-keeping or interbank deals. It is used by the Finance Ministry and customs for statistical purposes.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ROMANIA-LEU|LANGEN|Table|RDN|GNN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050912e19c001ch\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
