\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Romanian c.bank keeps  \highlight22\uc2 intervening \highlight\uc2  to tame leu  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Martin Dokoupil and Radu Marinas  \par \uc2 513 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 2005\par 11:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds analysts' comments, leu close)  \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Aug 16 (Reuters) - Romania's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) continued its battle against leu appreciation on Tuesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly on the market for the third day in a row, and, analysts said, fuelling uncertainty about its policy goals.  \par \par \uc2 The BNR has entered the market several times since Friday, buying around 300 million euros to keep the leu above 3.54 per euro despite its shift to inflation targeting, which analysts said should turn its focus onto interest rates rather than the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  creates uncertainty about BNR's policy objectives, especially given that the inflation targeting regime is so new and unproven in Romania," Danske Bank analyst Lars Christensen said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced on Monday it was shifting to an inflation targeting policy to fight rising prices better as the country moves closer to EU membership in 2007. It also said, however, it would keep managing the exchange rate.  \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, dealers said the BNR started to ask quotes when the leu hit highs of 3.5400 per euro and moved directly to buy euros in a range of 3.5700-3.5800 to counter firming pressure from exporters and remittances from Romanian workers abroad.  \par \par \uc2 The leu weakened as far as 3.5850/00 per euro after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . By the end of the session it had gradually regained some ground to close at 3.5550/50 against 3.5400/00 on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which rarely speaks about its market moves, declined to comment. "We don't make any comments on our market activities," BNR spokesman Mugur Stet told Reuters.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the BNR's move to switch from covert \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  via commercial banks to direct \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  was too aggressive, boosting volatility in the market and making it attractive for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators. "They are making their life difficult because after deciding to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as of last week they have basically drawn more speculative investment than in any of the last four or five months," ABN Amro senior analyst Radu Craciun said. "Any \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an excellent time to make money."  \par \par \uc2 Some economists said the BNR must be careful not to trigger a flood of hot money which could undermine its fight against stubborn inflation.  \par \par \uc2 "Every time they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...the more liquidity is pumped into the market and larger the chances for inflation down the road," Christensen said.  \par \par \uc2 The BNR did not drain money market liquidity via one-month deposit auctions since merging its key rates to a single 8.5 percent benchmark last week.  \par \par \uc2 Short-term money market rates fell to 3.8/6.8 percent from Monday's 6.4/8.2 percent.  \par \par \uc2 "They (the BNR) are in a learning process, because the market is not that developed. They should be as unpredictable as possible in terms of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if they want to scare off speculative investors," Christensen said.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ROMANIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 