\par\par \b \uc2 Romania - Factors to Watch on Aug 16  \b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 2005\par 08:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Aug 16 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Romanian financial markets on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 BRD REPORTS PROFIT RISE  \par \par \uc2 Private commercial bank BRD-SocGen, majority owned by France's Societe Generale recorded a net profit of 82.9 million euros ($102.7 million) in the first half this year, 97 percent up from the same 2004 period, financial paper Ziarul Financiar said.  \par \par \uc2 RAIFFEISEN NET PROFIT SOARS IN H1  \par \par \uc2 Raiffeisen Bank Romania recorded a net profit of 17.4 million euros in the first half of the year, four times higher than in the same 2004 period, financial newspaper Bursa said.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ROMANIA CENTRAL BANK INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\uc2  ON \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  MARKET  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at midday on Monday, buying euros to check a fast leu appreciation, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL15436859]  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  SHIFTS TO INFLATION TARGETING  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday announced a shift to inflation targeting to strengthen its fight against rising consumer prices as the country moves closer to European Union entry.  \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL15402644]  \par \par \uc2 BUDGET SURPLUS FLAT AT 0.4 PCT OF GDP  \par \par \uc2 Romania's consolidated budget surplus stayed flat at 0.4 percent of gross domestic at the end of June from end-May, the Finance Ministry said on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL15548174]  \par \par \uc2 NOTE - For a diary of forthcoming Romanian