\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Romanian c.bank buys euros to temper leu rise  \b0\par\par\uc2 214 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 2005\par 13:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, background)  \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Aug 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at midday on Monday, buying euros to check a fast leu appreciation, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "It (the BNR) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in waves when the leu hit bids of 3.4500," said one dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest. "It acted directly, and the unit stabilised at about 3.5800/50."  \par \par \uc2 The leu now trades at around 3.5700/00 against the euro. On Friday, it closed at 3.5390/50 against Thursday's 3.4570/25.  \par \par \uc2 The BNR's move came almost at the same time as the official announcement of its shift to inflation-targeting -- which should limit the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's powers to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and focuses mainly on rates.  \par \par \uc2 Operators said the leu started the day stronger due to increased hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  supply from clients and retail bureaux unloading remittances mainly from Romanians workers abroad, who returned home for the summer holiday.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers put the size of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at about 70 million euros ($86.70 million).  \par \par \uc2 BNR officials were not immediately available to comment.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ROMANIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RDN|GNN|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument 