\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 4- \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2  moves to inflation targeting,restrains leu  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Radu Marinas  \par \uc2 696 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 2005\par 09:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analyst comment)  \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Aug 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday announced a shift to inflation targeting to strengthen its fight against rising consumer prices as the country moves closer to European Union entry.  \par \par \uc2 But while \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Mugur Isarescu gave details of the policy -- which switches focus from the exchange rate -- the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to stop a steep appreciation of the leu, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the bank risked undermining its own policy.  \par \par \uc2 "They're in a policy dilemma. There's a clear risk that they can undermine the credibility of inflation targeting policy by paying too much attention to what happens in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," said Danske Bank analyst Lars Christensen.  \par \par \uc2 Isarescu announced the central 2006 inflation target would be 5.0 percent with a 1 percent band and this year's target 7.5 percent, with the same band on either side. Year-on-year inflation was 9.3 percent in July, the same as end-2004.  \par \par \uc2 The governor said next year's target was conditional on the centrist government not hiking the value added tax (VAT) rate to 22 percent from 19 to boost state revenues.  \par \par \uc2 "We believe that next year's inflation will probably rise to 6.5 percent if the government raises VAT to 22 percent," he told a news conference.  \par \par \uc2 FIGHTING INFLATION  \par \par \uc2 The long-anticipated announcement marked the official shift from monetary to direct inflation targeting, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says will make fighting inflation more effective, enhance its policy transparency and reduce inflation expectations.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the targets were realistic but warned the bank must work hand in hand with the government, which must gradually raise energy prices to EU levels, for the policy to work.  \par \par \uc2 "Both this year's and next year's targets are attainable," said independent financial analyst Florian Libocor. "But I think the bank's mission to ensure lasting disinflation towards the desired levels would be eased if they continue to work together as a team with the government."  \par \par \uc2 Isarescu said the targets hinged on tight fiscal policy and warned the bank would not hesitate to resort to monetary tools to attain its goal.  \par \par \uc2 "By all means, Romania must avoid granting further incentives that might boost demand," he said. "To reach its main objective (lasting price stability) the BNR will resort to all monetary policy instruments at its disposal."  \par \par \uc2 Economists say the policy shift, part of efforts to curb price growth in preparation for EU entry in 2007, should push the bank to allow the leu to strengthen.  \par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it will keep its managed-float regime for the leu for a few more years. In recent months, it has sporadically \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  through commercial banks to check the leu, which has appreciated by about 11 percent this year.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the bank moved directly on the market to keep the leu close to 3.53 to the euro, buying about 70 million euros on Monday. It was the second such intevention in consecutive trading days, after it bought 200 million euros on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The bank would not comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  but Isarescu said the bank would continue to move on the leu.  \par \par \uc2 "Romania cannot afford to give up its managed float at this time," Isarescu said. "When we \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  we don't have a specific exchange rate target. And it's well known that an excessive appreciation doesn't help disinflation and it could trigger credibility problems."  \par \par \uc2 But analysts said the bank should be careful because a strong presence in the market could backfire, making the leu attractive to speculators and luring hot money.  \par \par \uc2 "The idea is that massive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market boost unwanted volatility in the unit, thus creating the perfect playground for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators," Finansbank analyst Omer Tetik told Reuters.  \par \par \uc2 And Christensen added: "They must be very careful. They should not enter in a game with market forces, because they'll eventually lose."  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-ROMANIA-INFLATION (UPDATE 4)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|RDN|GNN|BNX|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050815e18f000eo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
