\par\par \b \uc2 Romania - Factors to Watch on Aug 15  \b0\par\par\uc2 403 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 2005\par 08:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Aug 15 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Romanian financial markets on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 OTP BANK ROMANIA REPORTS NET LOSS IN H1  \par \par \uc2 OTP Bank Romania, the local branch of Hungary's OTP Bank recorded net losses of 3.2 million euros ($3.99 million) in the first half this year, financial newspaper Ziarul Financiar said.  \par \par \uc2 UNITA RECORDS REVENUE GROWTH  \par \par \uc2 Insurance company Unita, a local branch of Wiener Staedtische has doubled its premium revenues to the equivalent of 38 million euros in the first half of the year, Ziarul Financiar said.  \par \par \uc2 HIGHER-THAN-PLANNED BUDGET GAP  \par \par \uc2 A higher-than-planned budget deficit of around one percent, of GDP in 2005, triggered mainly by floods which hit the country in April, May and in July, will not be negatively reflected in the upcoming EU's report on Romania's accession progress, Finance Minister Ionut Popescu was quoted as saying.  \par \par \uc2 DAEWOO UNIT  \par \par \uc2 Indebted carmaker Daewoo Automobile Romania has to pay a debt worth $5.59 million to local insurer Roumanie Assurance International, Ziarul Financiar reported.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ROMANIA CENTRAL BANK INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\uc2  ON \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  MARKET  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday, soaking up hefty hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  surpluses in a bid to cap a leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation against the euro.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the move was aimed at weakening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as much as possible before Monday, when the bank shifts to direct inflation targeting, which would limit its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  powers to increasingly focus on rates.  \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL12406341]  \par \par \uc2 ROMANIAN LEU ENDED WEAKER  \par \par \uc2 Romania's leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended weaker to the euro on Friday, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to check its rise.  \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL12544615]  \par \par \uc2 NOTE - For a diary of forthcoming Romanian events, double click [RO/DIARY], and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see [CONV/DIARY]. For other related news, double click on:   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  Romania Market Debt     [RO-DBT]   Romanian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       [RO-FRX]\par  Romania Market Report   [ROL/]     Romanian money      [RO-M]\par  Emerging Market Debt    [EMRG/DBT] Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     [EMRG/FRX]\par  All Emerging Markets news [EMRG]   CEE indicators  [CONV/DIARY]\par  All East Europe News       [EEU]   E.Europe equities     [.CEE]\par  TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets   [TOP/EMRG]\par  TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch  [TOP/EAST]\par  Romanian indicators        [RO/ECI]\par  Main page of Reuters poll  <RO/POLL1>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 LANGEN|Table|RDN|REVU|G|RBN|GNN|RNP|DNP|PGE|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050815e18f0009p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
