\par\par \b \uc2 Romanian leu flat, c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  suspected  \b0\par\par\uc2 378 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juli 2005\par 16:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, July 25 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's leu <EURRON=> closed flat in quiet trading on Monday after a suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  knocked it off its more than a five-month maximum of 3.5400 to the euro, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The leu firmed early on Monday as corporates sold hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but retreated back above 3.5500 in the middle of the day in what traders said looked like a covert \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BNR. It ended at 3.5490/45, unchanged from Friday.  \par \par \uc2 "The RON was appreciating in the morning until reaching 3.5400 (per euro)," one dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 "Then someone started buying euros and the exchange rate went up (weakened) to 3.5055. It could have been the NBR perhaps, because it happened at around noon ... as was the case last week," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The monetary body has been repeatedly trying to slow down quick rise of the leu with modest \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  through banks in July, saying it wanted to prevent excessive exchange rate moves. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials were not available to comment.  \par \par \uc2 The leu, which is up roughly 9.8 percent this year, resumed firming after its redenomination on July 1 as the BNR eased slightly its exchange rate policy, which had kept the unit locked above 3.6000 per euro since mid-March, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Market watchers expected firming pressure on the leu to continue in the coming days, but some said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would probably try to stabilise it at around 3.5500 per euro in the short term.  \par \par \uc2 Short-term money market rates were at 7.02/8.06 percent from Fridays 6.97/8.04 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The BNR drained 2.6 billion lei worth of one-month deposits from the market at an average rate of 8.0 percent <BNR13>.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  computed the indicative rate of the leu <FXRO01> at 3.5532 to the euro from 3.5579 on Friday. It was 2.9425 to the dollar from 2.9207. The rate is not compulsory for book-keeping or interbank deals. It is used by the Finance Ministry and customs for statistical purposes.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ROMANIA-LEU|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|RBN|RDN|GNN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050725e17p001f6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
