\par\par \b \uc2 Romanian leu flat, covert  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  suspected  \b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2005\par 19:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, July 19 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's leu <EURRON=> ended virtually unchanged to the euro in active trading on Tuesday, with some dealers suspecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  covertly again to prevent the unit's sharp appreciation.  \par \par \uc2 The leu closed at 3.5590/45 to the euro, its main reference \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in a client-driven session on Tuesday, compared with 3.5590/30 on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 "I suspect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to have been on the market today through a commercial bank," one dealer said. "It's more than a suspicion, because...there were some euro sales but someone bought exactly the (euro) surplus on the market."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR), which rarely comments on the exchange rate moves, has been suspected to purchase moderate volumes of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  via commercial banks over the past week to slow down the leu's rise.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said, however, more leu strengthening was on the cards in the coming days as investors would keep looking for a level, which would trigger a strong reaction from the BNR.  \par \par \uc2 Short-term money market rates ended at 6.97/8.0 percent from Monday's 7.5/8.0 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The BNR carried no open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday after draining 1.45 billion lei worth of one-month deposits from the market on Monday <BNR16>.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  computed the indicative rate of the leu <FXRO01> at 3.5632 to the euro versus 3.5635 on Monday. It was 2.9711 to the dollar from 2.9527. The rate is not compulsory for book-keeping or interbank deals. It is used by the Finance Ministry and customs for statistical purposes.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ROMANIA-LEU|LANGEN|Table|RDN|GNN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050719e17j001yd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
