\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2  cbank eyes prices, reserves for  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Antonia Oprita and Radu Marinas  \par \uc2 647 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2005\par 19:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Feb 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday it would keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to maintain stable prices and reserves, and was watching the leu's moves against the euro rather than a euro/dollar basket.  \par \par \uc2 In a rare confirmation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) drained euros to cool a firming leu, governor Mugur Isarescu said the bank bought more than 520 million euros from the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  interbank market over the past two days.  \par \par \uc2 "We will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the future," Isarescu told reporters. "Our goal is to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at an optimal level to cover five months of imports."  \par \par \uc2 "We do not have specific targets for the (leu's) exchange rate. Our objective is price stability," he added.  \par \par \uc2 The Balkan country has promised the International Monetary Fund to cut inflation, one of the highest in the region, to 7.0 percent this year from 9.3 percent in 2004.  \par \par \uc2 Until it shifted to a more flexible managed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  float last year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  used to announce forecasts on how much the leu was likely to appreciate in real terms against a euro/dollar basket with 75/25 weighting.  \par \par \uc2 The bank has been steadily reducing the dollar weighting in the basket as Romania prepares to join the European Union in 2007.  \par \par \uc2 Isarescu said the bank had switched to watching only the euro from the start of this year. "We weigh the leu a hundred percent against the euro from January the first."  \par \par \uc2 Isarescu said the BNR bought more than 220 million euros directly in the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week to cool the leu which has gained 12 percent this year reaching 34,900 to the euro. The bank also bought another 300 million euros indirectly from banks.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was looking to discourage speculators attracted by its plans to give foreigners access to leu deposits, a move expected to attract billions of euros in hot money.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sent a signal that it wishes to calm down the market," said financial analyst Florian Libocor.  \par \par \uc2 "It also tried to make the players understand that what's happening now on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market (the leu's fluctuations) is something we should all get used to," he added.  \par \par \uc2 GREATER EXCHANGE RATE FLEXIBILITY  \par \par \uc2 Isarescu did not want to say exactly when the next phase of capital account liberalisation would take place, but said greater flexibility of the exchange rate was likely to fend off speculative inflows.  \par \par \uc2 He did not offer any estimate of the hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows expected after the move, scheduled for the first half of this year. Some estimates have put the inflows at around 3 billion euros.  \par \par \uc2 Isarescu warned foreigners eager for quick gains that the bigger the hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows, the bigger the risk the small Romanian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market would not be able to absorb them. That could make the exchange rate unattractive.  \par \par \uc2 "They may want to come in with a long train, but we have quite a short platform for it," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said Isarescu's comments were also meant to signal to exporters, who have complained about the leu's strength over the past months, that they should become more competitive and that he was not worried about a bulging current account gap.  \par \par \uc2 "He is telling exporters to turn to products and services with more added value," said ABN Amro senior analyst Radu Craciun.  \par \par \uc2 Isarescu said foreign direct investments, including capital transfers, covered about 98 percent of last year's current account deficit of 7.7 percent of gross domestic product and that he saw exports rising by 10 percent this year. "I don't think Romania needs a major adjustment of the current account deficit this year because FDI is high," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050217e12h00611\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
