\par\par \b \uc2 Romanian Exporters Say Strong  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Is Hurting Jobs  \b0\par\par\uc2 215 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Februar 2005\par 12:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST (AP)--Exporters have urged \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tame the rise of the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the euro and the U.S. dollar, saying a strong leu endangered jobs and exports, newspapers reported Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Mihai Ionescu, executive director of the National Association of Exporters, was quoted by the daily Evenimentul Zilei as saying 90% of exporters experienced difficulties caused by the appreciation of the leu.  \par \par \uc2 "If the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the leu under a tighter leash, we will collapse," Ionescu was quoted as saying in Tuesday's edition. One million jobs in the export industry were under threat if the rise of the leu continued, he was quoted as saying.  \par \par \uc2 Ionescu couldn't be immediately reached by telephone.  \par \par \uc2 Traders speaking on condition of anonymity said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday,to dampen the rise of the leu.  \par \par \uc2 Since the beginning of the year, the leu has risen by 9.1% against the euro. The U.S. dollar has been in decline against the euro since the second half of last year.  \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has strengthened partly due to an estimated EUR2 billion to EUR3 billion sent home by Romanians working abroad. [ 15-02-05 1146GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050215e12f000jr\par }\page {\par\f