\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW-UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2  c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 fx \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  not ruled out.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Mirela Roman   \par \uc2 405 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 November 2004\par 13:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Nov 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) said on Wednesday it will limit but not scrap its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market a day after it moved to relax its managed float \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system.   \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday the BNR announced it will let the leu fluctuate in line with market trends, a major step towards opening up to short-term foreign capital inflows ahead of Romania's 2007 EU entry.   \par \par \uc2 It also cut its key interest rate, which it uses to drain money market funds, by 50 basis points to 18.25 percent.   \par \par \uc2 "It's important for the exchange rate to fully reflect market forces," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  vice-governor Cristian Popa told Reuters by telephone from Brussels.   \par \par \uc2 "The BNR has not completely eliminated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a possibility but you will see these limited. And of course the predictability of such \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be substantially lessened in the future," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Popa said a more flexible float, aimed at inflation targeting and ahead of freeing up capital flows early next year, would not have a "serious negative" impact on the current account gap, seen widening towards six percent of GDP this year.   \par \par \uc2 "We do not believe it will have serious negative consequences on the current account primarily because exports have a good performance despite real appreciation against the basket (so far this year) which is higher than the initial forecast of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Popa.   \par \par \uc2 "The current account performance can go up to close to six percent of GDP. That is independent of the change in the exchange rate policy as of yesterday," he added.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  move took the market by surprise and the leu rose to touch 39,430/50 against the euro. Dealers said the bank then stepped in to temper the leu's rise of about 2.5 percent since the announcement.   \par \par \uc2 Until Tuesday, the BNR had been steering the leu along a gradual course of appreciation through frequent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  under its managed float system.   \par \par \uc2 The policy change was also aimed at helping curb inflationary pressures, which have risen recently on the back of high world oil prices and demands for wage increases. Romania wants to cut inflation to under 10 percent this year, from 14.1 in 2003.   \par \par \uc2 "Our ultimate responsibility is inflation," Popa said. "That's the overriding goal of our policy."    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041103e0b3006lk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
