\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW-Romanian FinMin sees euro adoption 2012-2013.  \b0\par\par\uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 2004\par 12:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, May 11 (Reuters) - Romania, which hopes to join the European Union in 2007, will be able to adopt the euro sometime in 2012 or 2013, the ex-communist country's Finance Minister Mihai Tanasescu said on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Adrian Nastase said last month he hoped Romania will join the euro zone around 2010, earlier than a 2011-2013 timing estimated previously by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials.  \par \par \uc2 But Tanasescu said Romania would need more time.  \par \par \uc2 "I see euro adoption in five to six years after Romania joins the European Union," Tanasescu told Reuters in an interview. "It is a realistic view as our economy has to be ready for such a moment."  \par \par \uc2 Although Romania's budget deficits and public debt are well within the Maastricht criteria at present, the Balkan country has been slow to revamp its economy in 14 post-communist years.  \par \par \uc2 It is still striving to cut inflation, one of the highest in the region, to 9.0 percent this year from 14.1 percent in 2003.  \par \par \uc2 In the meantime, Romanians will slash some zeros from the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , now trading about 40,500 to the euro.  \par \par \uc2 Tanasescu said a long-awaited draft bill on a planned re-denomination - making the 10,000 "light" lei worth one "heavy" leu" - will be discussed by the government this week.  \par \par \uc2 Romanian bankers have repeatedly asked for a redenomination to ease bookeeping and costs of handling cash in circulation.  \par \par \uc2 "That move needs about 12 months of preparation, therefore the heavy leu will be on the market sometime between mid-2005 to early 2006," Tanasescu said.  \par \par \uc2 The leu, convertible on current account deals since 1998, will be fully liberalised on the capital account in 2007. \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a managed-float system, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  only in cases of increased volatility.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040511e05b0015p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
