\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Romania central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2  again as leu slides.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Radu Marinas and Antonia Oprita   \par \uc2 626 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 2003\par 15:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Nov 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) sold euros on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday for the third time in 10 days to temper a slide of the leu, caused mostly by seasonally high imports, dealers and analysts said.   \par \par \uc2 The leu was under pressure from a shortage of euros, triggered by both robust winter imports and a weakening dollar which prompted local traders to boost their euro positions, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 "It (the BNR) entered the market as the leu slid towards 40,020/60," said a dealer with a Bucharest bank. The unit, which closed at 39,955/995 to the euro on Friday firmed to 39,920/950 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and subsequently traded at 39,930/960.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers estimated Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 10 million euros.   \par \par \uc2 They said the BNR, which runs a managed-float system letting the leu move according to market demand but \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in cases of increased volatility, might have spent up to 50 million euros in its recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the slide of the leu, which is not traded internationally, was only temporary because after importers stock up for the harsh winter, expatriates' Christmas remittances will boost it again in December.   \par \par \uc2 "Today's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is surprising, given that the pressure on the leu is related not only to hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deficits but to the significant strengthening of the euro on world markets as well," ABN Amro senior analyst Radu Craciun said.   \par \par \uc2 "Traditionally, there is a surplus of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market in December," he added. "Companies sell hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to pay end-year taxes and bonuses, and Romanians working abroad send their savings home."   \par \par \uc2 LEU SLIDING   \par \par \uc2 He said the leu has depreciated 14.3 percent against the euro since the beginning of the year and 0.8 percent against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are aimed at stabilising the market," the BNR's communication manager Adrian Vasilescu told Reuters. He said the leu/euro rate "is now within the BNR programme".   \par \par \uc2 He dismissed media reports that the BNR was trying to prevent the euro from breaching through a 40,000 lei "psychological barrier".   \par \par \uc2 "There are no such barriers...We \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever the leu gets weaker too quickly or it firms too fast," Vasilescu said.   \par \par \uc2 Romania switched to the euro from the dollar as its reference \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March to reflect the weight of the euro zone in its foreign trade better.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said a stronger leu would not help reduce the country's bulging current account and trade deficits because it would contribute to a rise in imports.   \par \par \uc2 Romania's January-September trade deficit rose to $2.67 billion from $1.71 billion in the first nine months of last year, with year-on-year imports surging by 32.5 percent and exports by 28.7 percent.   \par \par \uc2 It has been the key factor in widening the current account gap by 48.1 percent to 1.395 billion euros ($1.64 billion) over January-August from the same 2002 period.   \par \par \uc2 The euro's strength on world markets has helped Romanian exports in 2002, when the country recorded a robust 4.9 percent GDP rise, mainly due to exports to its traditional trading partner, the European Union.   \par \par \uc2 The leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , convertible on current account deals since 1998, will be fully liberalised on the capital account in 2007, the year when Romania hopes to join the European Union.   \par \par \uc2 But analysts say this may open the leu to speculative attacks, a scenario already fought off this year by fellow EU candidate Hungary, even though \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  too could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  under its flexible exchange rate system.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031117dzbh002k3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
