\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Romania's c.bank sells euros to cushion leu fall.  \b0\par\par\uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 2003\par 17:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Nov 6 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  interbank market on Thursday, selling euros to temper a leu slide triggered by greater import-related demand, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers put the size of the BNR \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at about 15 million euros ($17 million) and said the leu's fall was a result of increased imports ahead of Romania's harsh winter and speculative pre-weekend trading by banks.  \par \par \uc2 They said it was not related to Romania's failure to get the EU's "functioning market economy" status in a European Commission report on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The leu, which is seen easing gradually in the days ahead, fell as low as 39,800/830 at midday, when the BNR \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It bounced back to 39,560/390 after the BNR move and ended at 39,620/650 against Wednesday's 39,670/700.  \par \par \uc2 "It's a medium-size \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  prompted by euro shortage on the market," one dealer with a private bank said. "There was no impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  side following the news (failure to get the EU's tag)."  \par \par \uc2 Latest BNR data show hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales to clients amounted to 63.8 million euro while buying from clients was 44.5 million euro on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 "The leu was depreciating too fast because the market was short," another dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 A London analyst said a sustained weakness of the leu could affect the country's inflation target.  \par \par \uc2 "If the weakness continues it could have some adverse implications for inflation," said Khatija Paruk, emerging markets analyst at Deutsche Bank in London.  \par \par \uc2 Romania aims to slash consumer price inflation, one of the highest in the region, to 14 percent this year and to a single digit in 2004 from 17.8 in 2002.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031106dzb6002wc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
