\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2  c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to slow leu fall-dealers. \b0\par\par\uc2 198 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 2000\par 12:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, May 23 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) sold dollars on the interbank market at midday on Tuesday to temper a faster downswing of the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  following some speculative plays in early trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The BNR stepped into the market to sell dollars after the leu weakened towards bids of 20,580," said one. \par \par \uc2  BNR officials were not immediately available for comment. \par \par \uc2  The leu recovered ground after the BNR move to trade near 20,545/55 against 20,580/95 at the opening but stayed softer than Monday's close of around 20,538/47. \par \par \uc2  Operators estimated the BNR's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at $10-15 million. They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  had also drained funds from the money market to check liquidity by posting bids at 34 percent on overnight, 37 percent on one week, 38 percent for two-weeks and 40 percent for one month. \par \par \uc2  Short-term money market rates were stable near 33/38 percent on overnight and 35/40 percent for one week. ((Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 312-0264, fax +40 1 315-8448, bucharest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw5n0002h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
