\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Weaker amid Slovak  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 879 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Dezember 1999\par 11:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 14 (Reuters) - Emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were slightly weaker on Tuesday as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Slovakia drew more attention than the dismissal of the Romanian prime minister. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Slovak crown\tab  , boosted to record highs against the euro amid hopes for increased foreign investment next year, eased only a touch after dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par The bank bid down the crown\tab      to 42.15 to the euro and then 42.20 after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in early trade hit its strongest level since the creation of the euro, at 42.087 according to Reuters data.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Soon after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  it was bid at 42.168 compared with 42.10 late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "I'm not sure how great a success they're going to have given the euro's broad-based weakness," said Jake Moore, emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Barclays Capital. "It (the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) will only be of limited impact." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's moves came despite Finance Minister Brigita Schmognerova saying on Monday she would prefer the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the end of the year as it could complicate exchange rate risks for companies. \par \par \uc2  Her comments boosted the crown to record levels, adding fuel to a rally driven in recent days by expectations the European Union's invitation for membership talks will boost foreign business investment in Slovakia. \par \par \uc2  ROMANIAN DISMISSAL \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Romania\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was also expected to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after resuming dollar purchases on Monday to prevent an appreciation of the leu\tab  .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par That prospect weakened the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the dollar and overshadowed the dismissal late on Monday of Prime Minister Radu Vasile.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Vasile was ousted following a revolt in his Christian Democrat party over slow economic reform and hopes that fresh leadership would speed admission to the EU.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The leu was bid weaker at 17,935 to the dollar from 17,895 on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The zloty\tab   continued to weaken amid dampened hopes for a fast decision on a full float of the zloty.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell to 1.08 percent stronger than the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's parity level, compared with 1.44 percent on Monday and more than two percent after comments by the finance minister last week triggered hopes for a quick move to a float.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Against the euro\tab      the zloty was bid at 4.221 to the euro from 4.212.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The focus is likely to shift to inflation on Wednesday, when consumer price data is expected to show annual inflation accelerated to 9.25 percent in November from 8.7 percent in October.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Czech third-quarter gross domestic product figures are also due on Wednesday, and expected to show about 0.7 percent growth from a year earlier.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The crown\tab \tab \tab was in the meantime little changed, bid at 35.86 to the euro against 35.88 on Monday.\par Hungary's forint\tab   showed little reaction to news consumer prices rose 10.6 percent year-on-year and 0.4 percent month-on-month in November, broadly in line with market expectations.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was bid at 2.22 percent above parity, just off Monday's close at the 2.25 percent strong end of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  band.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ** Following is a table of key emerging market exchange rates,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par including the change versus late New York trade the previous day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and the change in the year to date.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ** The Czech, Polish, Hungarian and Slovak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , formerly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quoted against the mark, are now quoted against the euro to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reflect new market norms. All other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are quoted\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ** According to market convention, exchange rates are quoted in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par units per dollar or euro and the percentage change denotes the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rise or fall of the dollar or euro value.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ** Annual percentage changes are calculated from late on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par first day of the current trading year, January 4.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab    LATEST  PREV    PCT CHG  PCT CHG\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab  CLOSE\tab \tab in 1999\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EUROPE/MEAST/AFRICA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Czech Rep.\tab \tab    35.86   35.90   -0.11%  3.04%\par Poland\tab \tab \tab  4.22    4.21    0.20%   3.69%\par Hungary\tab \tab \tab 253.7   254.20  -0.20%  1.00%\par Slovakia\tab \tab      42.16   42.10   0.14%   -1.95%\par Romania\tab \tab \tab 17,935  17,895  0.22%   63.79%\par Ukraine\tab \tab \tab 5.40    5.40    0.00%   37.40%\par South Africa\tab \tab  6.13    6.12    0.13%   4.79%\par Kenya\tab \tab \tab   74.65   74.50   0.20%   21.19%\par Israel\tab \tab \tab  4.193   4.199   -0.14%  1.79%\par Turkey\tab \tab \tab  527,970 526,490 0.28%   67.21%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par LATAM\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mexico\tab \tab \tab  9.41    9.40    0.02%   -4.42%\par Brazil\tab \tab \tab  1.8500  1.8500  0.00%   53.26%\par Venezuela\tab \tab     642.00  642.00  0.00%   13.73%\par Chile\tab \tab \tab   538.10  538.10  0.00%   14.44%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ASIA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore\tab \tab     1.678   1.678   0.01%   1.31%\par Hong Kong\tab \tab     7.774   7.775   -0.01%  0.36%\par China\tab \tab \tab   8.279   8.280   0.00%   0.00%\par Indonesia\tab \tab     7,205   7,230   -0.35%  -9.37%\par Thailand\tab \tab      38.53   38.54   -0.03%  6.73%\par Philippines\tab \tab   40.64   40.65   -0.02%  5.97%\par Taiwan\tab \tab \tab  31.63   31.50   0.41%   -1.46%\par South Korea\tab \tab   1,133   1,128   0.44%   -4.39%\par India\tab \tab \tab   43.53   43.46   0.16%   2.45%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvce08fnz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal276