\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  To Halt Leu Fast Fall-Dealers \b0\par\par\uc2 247 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 1999\par 14:08\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST -(Dow Jones)- The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, selling dollars to halt the leu's (ROL) fast fall, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came as the dollar was quoted at between ROL17,950 and ROL18,010, up from between ROL17,900 and ROL17,950 at the opening Monday. \par \par \uc2  After the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar was quoted at between ROL17,790 and ROL17,870. The leu resumed its depreciation trend quickly and was traded at between ROL17,870 and ROL17,950. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market, where it attracted one-week leu deposits with a 70% interest rate. The bank's move was aimed at reducing leu liquidity to limit commercial bank placements in dollars. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers estimated the leu would continue to fall in the coming days, albeit at a lower pace. They said the leu's depreciation is caused mainly by speculative trade from banks. \par \par \uc2  The leu fell by 2.6% last week, and dealers said the leu's depreciation has been also encouraged by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  So far, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  supported a gradual depreciation of the leu, which is expected to help the country to reduce its current account deficit to less than $1.5 billion this year from about $3 billion in 1998. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; czan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010827dvbm005n9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
