\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2  c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to ease pressure on leu. \b0\par\par\uc2 212 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 1999\par 13:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Nov 22 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at midday on Monday, selling dollars to temper a faster depreciation of the leu, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They also said the BNR had also stepped into the money market to soak up one-week deposits at rates near 70 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The BNR entered the market after the leu weakened towards 17,900/960 to the dollar," said a dealer with a foreign bank. "It sold dollars at 17,890 to 17,810." \par \par \uc2  The leu firmed a bit towards quotes of 17,800/900 after the BNR moves. The unit opened the day softer at 17,890/950 against 17,790/900 at last Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  Traders were reluctant to estimate the size of the BNR \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  side. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials were not immediately available for comments. \par \par \uc2  The leu faced increased pressure starting last week due to speculative trading by banks. It lost nearly three percent against the dollar last week although its fall had been temporarily capped by Friday's BNR money market drainages. ((Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 312-0264, fax +40 1 315-8448, bucharest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbm09hzk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
