\par\par \b \uc2  Romanian Leu Steady Vs Dlr Early; Slight Rise Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 237 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 1999\par 09:15\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is steady against the dollar early Friday, with dealers predicting a slight appreciation during the session due to corporate demand for lei. \par \par \uc2  At 0700 GMT, the dollar was between ROL15,955 and ROL15,975, unchanged from late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Market participants expect demand for dollar to be lower over the session amid increasing leu demand from companies that need funds for end of the month payments. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in the market to buy dollars in order to prevent a substantial appreciation of the leu, dealers said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials said earlier a stronger leu would encourage imports, however the country's current account deficit would widen. They said the leu would depreciate in line with inflation. \par \par \uc2  In June, inflation rose 5.1% on the month, following a 5.3% raise in May. \par \par \uc2  On the money market, interest rates dropped sharply, while liquidity rose after the Finance Ministry rejected bids for Treasury bills earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  The overnight money market rate was quoted early Friday at between 0% and 30%, down from between 50% and 70% Thursday, while the one-week deposit rate was quoted at between 20% and 40%, from between 60% and 110% Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  23-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0715GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010827dv7n003oa\par }\pag