\par\par \b \uc2  Romanian Leu Lower Vs Dlr Early; Seen Slightly Lower \b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 1999\par 09:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is lower against the dollar early Thursday amid dollar demand from banks, and is seen falling slightly by the end of the day. \par \par \uc2  At 0720 GMT, the dollar was trading between ROL15,910 and ROL15,930, up from between ROL15,875 and ROL15,895 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Market participants said the leu fell in early trading as some banks bought dollars to fill their hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions ahead of weekend. They also said the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to buy dollars in order to restore its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which were depleted to around $852 million at the end of June due to heavy foreign debt payments. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might encourage a depreciation of the leu in line with inflation, to prevent a real appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Romanian inflation rose 5.1% in June on the month, compared with a rise of 5.3% in May, the National Commission for Statistics said Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Year-on-year inflation at the end of June was 48.2%. \par \par \uc2  Dealers' attention will continue to be focused on the money market, ahead of an increase in commercial banks' minimum reserve requirements to 20% from 15% on July 16. \par \par \uc2  Market participants said that interest rates are expected to go up following the increase in minimum reserve requirements, as banks will need time to adapt to the higher level. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the overnight money market rate was quoted between 15% and 30%, while the one-week deposit rate was quoted between 35% and 60%. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 15-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0737GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7f05cyf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
