\par\par \b \uc2  Romanian Leu Slightly Up Vs Dlr Early; Seen Stable \b0\par\par\uc2 213 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 1999\par 09:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is slightly higher against the dollar early Friday and is seen ending the session around its current levels, market players said. \par \par \uc2  At 0650 GMT, the dollar was trading between ROL15,835 and ROL15,855, down from between ROL15,840 and ROL15,865 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The calm and thin trading conditions early Friday suggest little change for the leu over the day. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in recent days to fine tune liquidity in an effort to maintain low interest rates for leu deposits. \par \par \uc2  Low interest rates would enable the finance ministry to sell its Treasury bills at lower yields to finance the public debt. Until now, the finance ministry had to sell T-bills at expensive yields, quoted around 100%. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers said money market rates are expected to rise again after July 16, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new minimum reserve requirements come into force, as banks need some time to adapt to the higher levels. \par \par \uc2  Commercial banks' minimum reserve requirements will rise to 20% from 15% on July 16. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; 401 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 09-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0710GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv79056dk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
