\par\par \b \uc2  Romanian Leu Up Vs Dlr Early; Slight Appreciation Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 220 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 1999\par 09:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is slightly higher against the dollar early Thursday and is seen continuing to appreciate slowly as dollar supply more than meets demand, market participants said. \par \par \uc2  At 0720 GMT, the dollar was trading between ROL15,820 and ROL15,840, down from between ROL15,830 and ROL15,850 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the leu may continue its rally against the dollar over the session amid low dollar demand. They said that if the dollar goes below ROL15,800, the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to buy the dollar surplus. \par \par \uc2  "A stronger leu is not welcomed now, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will prevent any major appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a dealer at a foreign bank in Bucharest said. A stronger leu would encourage imports, increasing the trade deficit and, ultimately, the current account deficit, he added. \par \par \uc2  Romania has pledged to reduce the current account deficit to $2 billion this year, from about $3 billion in 1998. \par \par \uc2  In the money market Thursday, the overnight rate was between 30% and 50%, while the rate for one-week deposits was between 50% and 75%. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 01-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0745GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7104z0e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\pic