\par\par \b \uc2  Romanian Leu Lower Vs Dlr Early; Further Fall Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 266 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 April 1999\par 09:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is slightly lower against the dollar early Monday, and dealers are predicting it could continue to fall during the day. \par \par \uc2  At 0725 GMT, the dollar was between ROL14,850 and ROL14,950, up from between ROL14,800 and ROL14,880 late Friday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the leu is likely to depreciate further by the end of the day amid increasing dollar demand. But they said the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the leu. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , selling small amounts of dollars above the ROL15,000 level. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also attracted leu deposits at high rates to divert banks from investing in the dollar. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the overnight money market rate was quoted between 80% and 130%, while the rate for one-week deposits was quoted between 100% and 170%. \par \par \uc2  The deputy governor of the Romanian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Cristian Popa, said Saturday that the bank will continue its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market to defend the leu against speculative attacks. \par \par \uc2  Popa said he believed the leu is now at "equilibrium levels." \par \par \uc2  Market observers said the leu might become more stable in the coming weeks after the government agrees with the International Monetary Fund on a new financial agreement for Romania. \par \par \uc2  The government is expected to sign a memorandum of understanding with the IMF for a $450 million stand-by loan Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 19-04-99 \par \par \uc2  0742GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv4j02x9c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
