\par\par \b \uc2  EBRD/ \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2  Central Banker -2: Won't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 1999\par 15:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  International bankers have speculated that \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  may try to raise short-term loans by pledging its gold reserves, which are worth an estimated $900 million, as collateral. But Popa said that under the terms of its Samurai bond issue, which matures on May 28, the government can't use its gold for this purpose. \par \par \uc2  Popa said the bank may instead deposit some of its gold overseas in order to earn some interest. \par \par \uc2  Although Popa earlier pledged that the country wouldn't default on its bonds and would try to protect its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the country's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets are expected to be volatile throughout May and June. \par \par \uc2  But speaking to Dow Jones Newswires, Popa said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will confine itself to periodic \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money markets. \par \par \uc2  "We don't want to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, since that would involve a lot of reserves," he said. "We will continue to do what we have been doing up till now and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market to defend against speculative attacks." \par \par \uc2  By raising short-term interest rates, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can limit the availability of leu (ROL) with which to buy dollars. \par \par \uc2  Popa said he believed the leu is now at "equilibrium levels." \par \par \uc2  In addition to loans from the IMF, the World Bank and foreign banks, Popa hopes the government will be able to ease its financial problems through sales of state-owned companies for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Popa estimated that the government will receive between $1.4 billion and $1.5 billion from this source in 1999. \par \par \uc2  Popa told Dow Jones Newswires that the crisis in Kosovo won't affect the government's ability to reach that target. \par \par \uc2  "Some investor prudence is warranted, but I don't see sizable adverse effects (from Kosovo)," he said. \par \par \uc2  Other countries affected by the Kosovo crisis are less optimistic. A Bulgarian government minister Friday said he expects foreign direct investment in the country to be halved as a result of the war. \par \par \uc2  -Paul Hannon 44-411-423 651 paul.hannon@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 17-04-99 \par \par \uc2  1316GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv4h02wcz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
